Unions that overlay bytes or bitfields on a wider integer. GCC/clang on a
little-endian target allocate bitfields and bytes from the least
significant end, MWCC on PowerPC from the most significant end, so the
member order is reversed for the host to keep each name on the same bits
of the integer. GameAudio::Main::isActive reads the named bit instead of
masking the packed byte. JAUAudience.h also keeps the inline bodies when
JAUAUDIENCE_EXTERN_DEFINITIONS is set, since the out-of-line copies are
an MWCC weak-emission trick.

